===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*bʰeh₂-|id=speak}}
From {{der|en|enm|ben}}, {{m|enm|bene}}, from {{der|en|ang|bēn||prayer, request, favor, compulsory service}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*bōniz||supplication}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*bʰeh₂-||to say}}. Related to {{l|en|ban}}. More at {{l|en|boon}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|en|bene}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A [[prayer]]; a [[petition]].

===Etymology 2===
From {{der|en|enm|ben}}, {{m|enm|bene}}, variation of {{m|enm|bin}}, {{m|enm|binne||within}}, from {{der|en|ang|binnan||within, in, inside of, into}}, equivalent to {{prefix|en|be|in}}.

====Preposition====
{{en-prep}}

# {{lb|en|Scotland|northern England}} [[in|In]], [[into]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2008|author=w:James Kelman|title=Kieron Smith, Boy|page=32|publisher=Penguin|year_published=2009
|passage=And he was waving to me to creep in, so I just did and then just to skip '''ben''' the front and then in the lobby.}}

====Adverb====
{{en-adv|-}}

# {{lb|en|Scotland|Northern England}} [[inside|Inside]].

====Adjective====
{{en-adj|er|sup=benmost}}

# Inner, [[interior]].

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|en|ben-end}}, {{l|en|ben-room}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|Scotland|Northern England}} The inner [[room]] of a two-room [[cottage]] (as opposed to the [[but]]); the [[ben room]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1972|author={{w|George Mackay Brown}}|title=Greenvoe|publisher=Polygon|year_published=2019|page=25
|passage=Bert Kerston was awakened by a steady tap on the '''ben''' window.}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|en|but and ben}}

=====References=====
* [http://www.dsl.ac.uk/entry/snd/ben_adv_prep_adj_n1 The Dictionary of the Scots Language]

