{{head|srn|particle}}

# {{n-g|Verbal marker for the past tense.}}

====Usage notes====
This marker can be combined with the markers {{m|srn|sa}} or {{m|srn|o}} for the future tense and {{m|srn|e}} for the progressive aspect, in which case the order, if all are used, is that of ''ben sa/o e''. Some examples:
* ''mi ben waka'': “I had walked”.
* ''mi ben e waka'': “I was walking”.
* ''mi ben sa waka'': “I would walk”.
* ''mi ben sa e waka'': “I would have been walking”.

